 "l70-d1-n8-ngl50": {
  "tps": 18.17732767747163,
  "n": 374,
  "text": "```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Merge overlapping intervals in a list of [start, end] pairs and return the merged list sorted by start.\n\n    Args:\n        intervals: A list of intervals, where each interval is a list of two integers, [start, end].\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of merged intervals, sorted by start.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n\n    # Sort intervals by start\n    intervals.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    merged = [intervals[0]]\n    for current in intervals[1:]:\n        # Get the last merged interval\n        last_merged = merged[-1]\n\n        # Check if the current interval overlaps with the last merged interval\n        if current[0] <= last_merged[1]:\n            # Merge the current interval with the last merged interval\n            merged[-1] = [last_merged[0], max(last_merged[1], current[1])]\n        else:\n            # Add the current interval to the merged list\n            merged.append(current)\n\n    return merged\n\n# Example calls\nprint(merge_intervals([[1, 3], [2, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]))  # [[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]\nprint(merge_intervals([[1, 4], [4, 5]]))  # [[1, 5]]\nprint(merge_intervals([[1, 2], [3, 5], [6, 7], [8, 10], [12, 16]]))  # [[1, 2], [3, 5], [6, 7], [8, 10], [12, 16]]\n```",
